       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and arrhythmia. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't make it safe.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n- **100 mg** by mouth once daily, which is a common maintenance dose.\n- **200 mg** by mouth once daily, which is the maximum.\n- **50 mg** by mouth once daily, which is the usual starting dose.\n\nIf 1000 mg is intentional, for example as part of a specific protocol, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
